A||||9||Joe Torma||No Happiness in 3400Land||||8||
Z||000000||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||09:55 PM||||Well I guess this is a Technical gripe.<P>Its been about 2 months since I have started my new 3400 conversion.  It has an aftermarket engine control system for those who don't know.  Anyway.<P>I fixed some wiring and started it.<BR>Took 2 tries and she fired up. It was running pretty good...so I looked at my laptop to check out the sensor values.  "Why is my voltage dropping???"  Well it seems my new 220amp alternator may spin the wrong way.  Aaarrgg.  <P>Put the charger on, restart. Runs for a while, but it's got a miss. Stalls.  Starts and stalls a bunch of times.  Out of gas.  Put some gas in.  Runs now and there's a miss from both banks.<P>Guess I'll be pulling plugs tomorrow.<BR>This sucks.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">    <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||10:42 PM||||Eh...I guess I shouldn't listen to people "helping" me--alternator is spinning the correct way.  Its a little late tonight to try this, but does the allternator idiot light have to be functioning for the alternator to work.  The wiring diagram shows 12v going through the lamp to the brown wire on the alternator.  Is this another "turn on" wire?<P>Anyone have a lamp burn out and the alternator not work from that?<P>TIA,<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fformula88||09-07-2001||10:43 PM||||Sorry to hear about the bad luck so far... but your going to forget all these troubles as soon as you have the car up and running.  Stomping on the gas will make all these frustrations go away!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||09-07-2001||10:50 PM||||I grabbed a schematic and the alternator has 2 brown wires- one goes to the failure lamp and the other is the regulator "excitor" lead that is a 12v switched connection. In the plug, the excitor lead is closest to the big side of the plug.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||11:04 PM||||Hmmm...ok, I've got a new connector on that alternator. In that I have a red, brown and black.  I assume that the turn on is red, the idjit lamp is brown, and ground is black.  There is no juice in the brown wire right now, because I have the dash out...and from your schematic it looks like the brown has 12V from the fuse block, right?<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||DRH||09-07-2001||11:32 PM||||Ok, The Haynes manual shows a total of 3 wires. The big red one that screws on, a Red and a brown that plug in. The smaller red is always hot same as the big Red. The brown runs back to the idiot bulb.<P>My 88 has a total of 4 wires. The big red one and 3 on a plug. The red and brown are the same but it also has a brown/white that goes to the Fan E Fuse, Hot in Run.<P>Alt. usually ground thru the casing. I suspect the black wire is for another purpose. Where'd you get the Alt? Does it have any wiring diagrams?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||11:51 PM||||I got it from Mr.Alternator.<BR>No diagrams.  I figured that the alts do get grounded through the case, but black is usually ground 99% of the time...this is a pretty high amp unit so maybe it takes a special ground.  I'm going to plug that idiot light in tomorrow and see if it work.<P>So far its wired right...that black wire is questionable though.<P>Thanks||||reg||4
Z||000007||Joe Torma||09-07-2001||11:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>The red and brown are the same but it also has a brown/white that goes to the Fan E Fuse, Hot in Run.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wait a minute...<BR>If that turn on(red) is constantly hot...the regulator would be active all the time, and drain the battery.  That brown wire is switched 12v...the real turn on?  I betcha it needs that idiot light to work.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DRH||09-08-2001||12:15 AM||||That makes sense. It could explain why they added the extra wire on my 88 too. Since the extra wire is switched it could let the altenator work even if the bulb burns out. <P>Good luck.||||reg||3
Z||000009||Joe Torma||09-08-2001||12:38 PM||||Yup...gotta have the idjit light working.<BR>Good to know huh?!<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A> ||||reg||1
